  data:  # aac9
    kind: work_item  # aac9
    title: "Python analyzer: module-level NAME = ... assignments not indexed as Symbols; 151 ALL-CAPS externals on hypergumbo (E2 of WI-davan split)"  # aac9
    status: todo_hard  # aac9
    priority: 2  # aac9
    parent:  # aac9
    tags:  # aac9
    - analysis_quality  # aac9
    isbefore: []  # aac9
    duplicate_of: []  # aac9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # aac9
    pr_ref:  # aac9
    description: "Split off from WI-davan-disis-jamag-bubol-buzaf-homul-mijik-gakoz on\n2026-04-24 per its drill-down discussion note dated 2026-04-24T23:21:37Z. The\noriginal WI-davan filing attributed 9 specific externals to a monorepo\n`src/` layout bug; the drill-down found that those 9 are a subset of a larger\nclass of 151 externals driven by an independent root cause documented here.\nWI-davan is now scoped to E1 (layout detection); this item is E2.\n\n## Symptom\n\nModule-level `NAME = ...` assignments are not indexed as Symbols by the Python\nanalyzer. Verified by listing all `taxonomy.py` Symbol kinds on hypergumbo\nself-analysis:\n\n```\nmethod=53, class=12, function=8, module=1\nconstants=0\n```\n\n…yet `taxonomy.py` clearly defines `LANGUAGE_ALIASES`, `LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS`,\n`SOURCE_EXTENSIONS` at module scope.\n\nWhen `from .taxonomy import LANGUAGE_ALIASES` runs through the resolver:\n1. Relative import resolves to `(module=taxonomy, name=LANGUAGE_ALIASES)`.\n2. `_lookup_symbol_by_module(global_symbols, \"taxonomy\", \"LANGUAGE_ALIASES\")` — MISS\n   (constant not indexed).\n3. Fall through to external — `create_boundary_nodes` synthesises a tier-3\n   `external_symbol` node.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`py.py` has a `_collect_module_constants` helper at line 842, but it is used\nonly for internal URL-path resolution in route decorators (`py.py:2118`). It\nnever emits `Symbol` objects into the `symbols` list that becomes\n`global_symbols`. So the resolver has no way to find module-level constants\nacross files.\n\n## Scope\n\n**151 ALL-CAPS constant-shaped externals on hypergumbo self-analysis**:\nPASS_VERSION, SCHEMA_VERSION, DEFAULT_EXCLUDES, EXIT_SUCCESS,\nEXIT_USER_ERROR, CHARS_PER_TOKEN, EXCLUDED_KINDS, LANGUAGE_ALIASES,\nLANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS, SOURCE_EXTENSIONS, …\n\nSome entries appear duplicated — one `python:hypergumbo_core.X:0-0:NAME:symbol`,\none `python:packages.hypergumbo-core.src.hypergumbo_core.X:0-0:NAME:symbol` —\nbecause some callers write absolute imports (`from hypergumbo_core.ir import\nPASS_VERSION`) and others relative (`from .ir import PASS_VERSION`). E1\n(WI-davan) makes the relative-import path derive a different path-shaped\nqualifier than the absolute one, so each external resolution miss produces a\ndistinct synthetic node. Once E2 lands, E1's qualifier shape becomes the only\nremaining issue and *both* paths resolve to the same indexed constant.\n\nBeyond hypergumbo, every Python repo that exports module-level constants (very\ncommon — config dictionaries, sentinel values, version strings, framework\nregistries) will have an analogous undercount of resolved `imports`/`reads`\nedges and a corresponding overcount of tier-3 externals.\n\n## Fix direction\n\n1. Extend the Python analyzer's symbol-extraction pass to emit\n   `Symbol(kind=\"constant\", …)` for module-level `ast.Assign` and\n   `ast.AnnAssign` nodes whose target is a `Name`. Reuse the\n   `_collect_module_constants` walk logic.\n2. Register `constant` in the IR `Symbol.kind` allowlist (if one exists; this\n   may be a separate IR change governed by `schema.py`).\n3. Update `_lookup_symbol_by_module` to look up constants by `(module, name)`\n   alongside functions/classes.\n4. Decide whether `ast.AugAssign` (`X += ...` at module scope) and tuple\n   targets (`A, B = 1, 2`) are in scope. Recommend yes for tuple unpacking,\n   no for AugAssign (rare at module scope, semantically a mutation).\n\nOptional: emit `is_dunder=True` meta for `__all__`, `__version__`, etc., so\ndownstream consumers can distinguish framework-significant constants from\nordinary module-scope state.\n\n## Scope expansion / invariants\n\n- Same gap likely exists in JS/TS (`export const X = ...` at module scope),\n  Ruby (top-level constants), and other dynamic-language analyzers. File\n  separately if confirmed.\n- Candidate invariant: \"Every module-level binding that can be the target of\n  `from <mod> import <name>` MUST be indexed as a Symbol.\" Currently violated\n  for Python module-level Assign / AnnAssign.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```bash\nhypergumbo run . --out /tmp/hg.json\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nnodes = json.load(open('/tmp/hg.json'))['nodes']\next = [n for n in nodes\n       if (n.get('meta') or {}).get('external_boundary')\n       and n.get('language') == 'python'\n       and (n.get('name') or '').isupper()]\nprint('ALL-CAPS python externals:', len(ext))\nfor n in ext[:20]: print(' ', n['id'])\n\"\n```\n\nExpected before fix: ~150 hits including PASS_VERSION, SCHEMA_VERSION, etc.\nExpected after fix: near-zero.\n\n## Validation\n\nTag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time. Claim to validate: \"ALL-CAPS\nexternal_symbol nodes in `python:` namespace drop from ~150 to near-zero on\nhypergumbo self-analysis.\" Cross-validate on a second Python repo that\nexports module-level constants heavily (django, fastapi, click).\n\n## Relationship to E1 (WI-davan)\n\nIndependent. E1 is in `_detect_src_layout` (py.py:1471); E2 is in\nsymbol-extraction (py.py:842 helper, currently unused for Symbol emission).\nEither may land first. Until both land, the duplicated `python:hypergumbo_core.X`\nvs `python:packages.hypergumbo-core.src.hypergumbo_core.X` external pairs will\npersist."  # aac9
    fields: {}  # aac9
